  gallery={gallery}
  prev={{ href: '/swans-market/', label: "Swan's Market" }}
  next={{ href: '/hunziker-areal/', label: 'Hunziker Areal' }}
>
  <section class="case-reading mx-auto max-w-[820px] px-6 pt-12 sm:px-12">
    <p>Vauban is a Freiburg district, not one cooperative or one courtyard. The city describes a roughly 41-hectare neighborhood for about 5,500 people, with housing, schools, services, green spaces and low-energy building requirements. Tram service reached the district in 2006. <a class="source-link" href="https://www.freiburg.de/pb/208736.html">[Project source]</a></p>
    <p>Many households live without a private car; parking arrangements concentrate much private-car storage in district garages. That is different from claiming every vehicle is banned. Deliveries, emergency access and people with differing mobility needs remain parts of an inhabited neighborhood.</p>
    <h2>A good block needs a way out.</h2>
    <p>The courtyard may be the place to linger, but work, school, friends and appointments are elsewhere too. Reliable transport and useful nearby services determine whether lower car ownership is practical. A bicycle room is excellent; it cannot substitute for an accessible daily journey.</p>
    <p>At district scale, the coordination work grows: street networks, transit funding, schools, utilities, land allocation and long-term public maintenance. A diagram of repeated courtyards should show those institutions, not make them disappear.</p>
    <aside class="research-note mt-8">Reading lens: project publications document the place and its intended design. They are not independent evaluations of affordability, energy performance or how every resident experiences life there. The questions here are our interpretation.</aside>
  </section>

  <Fragment slot="lessons">
<li>Plan daily trips with residents who have different ages, schedules and mobility needs.</li>
<li>Treat public transport and services as funded projects, not labels on a master plan.</li>
<li>Distinguish the district’s policies from the tenure or performance of any one building.</li>
</Fragment>

  <Fragment slot="sources"><a href="https://www.freiburg.de/pb/208736.html">City of Freiburg · Vauban district overview</a>. Reviewed October 2026. Approximate counts are identified; population changes over time.</Fragment>
</CaseStudy>
